-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",224,{
[7137]="7002C9D5\n1\tTalk to Gadda\tGadda is outside of the Mead Hall at Stangard.\n2\tTalk to Stanric inside his house\tStanric is inside of his house in Stangard, near the Mead Hall.\n3\tTell Stanric of your methods and hear his thoughts\tStanric is in his household near the Mead Hall.\n4\tTalk to Stanric\tTalk to Stanric.\n5\tFollow Stanric outside\tStanric has gone outside. You should follow him.\n6\tTalk to Gadda\tGadda is outside of Stanric's house.\n7\tObserve the confrontation between Sithric and Stanric\tGadda, Stanric, and Sithric are outside of the Mead Hall.\n8\tTalk to Stanric\tTalk to Stanric.\n",
[7138]="7001ABB7\n1\tDefeat Gúlbenn, the sorcerer of Minas Gîl\030Defeat Twilight atop Minas Gîl\tDefeat the sorcerer Gúlbenn and his servants atop Minas Gîl.\n",
[7139]="700385FE\n1\tTalk to Éowyn\tÉowyn is standing outside the Mead Hall of Entwade. You should speak to Lady Éowyn and drive the White Hand from Entwade.\n2\tFollow Éowyn\tÉowyn can be found near the Mead Hall of Entwade. You should follow Éowyn.\n3\tAid Agelman and Éowyn in defending Entwade\tThane Edric's men can be found to the east of the Mead Hall of Entwade. You should aid Agelman and Éowyn in combat.\n4\tTalk to Anrad\tAnrad can be found at the gate of Entwade near the Sutcrofts. You have defended the southern flank of Entwade and should now secure the gate.\n5\tDefeat Orcs attacking the palisades of Entwade\tMordor Orcs can be found outside the gates of Entwade, hacking at the nearby fences. Anrad has asked that you slip past the Orcs at the gate and engage Orcs attacking the walls of Entwade.\n6\tFind Síric\tSíric can be found in northern Entwade with Womar and Gifel. You should seek out Síric and aid him.\n7\tTalk to Síric\tSíric is in northern Entwade. You have discovered Síric and his men amidst slain White Hand forces. You should speak to Síric.\n8\tFollow Éowyn to the western flank\tÉowyn and the others can be found to the west. Éowyn is running toward the western flank of Entwade. You should follow her.\n9\tDefeat Nâdar\tNâdar can be found at the western edge of Entwade. You have encountered the leader of the White Hand forces in Entwade. You should defeat him.\n10\tTalk to Éowyn\tÉowyn can be found inside Entwade in eastern Kingstead. You have repelled the White Hand and brought some measure of peace to the Wade. You should now speak to Éowyn.\n",
[7140]="7002FD21\n1\tObserve the small creatures in Ashlimb's memory\tYou should pay heed to the Ent's vision.\n2\tReturn to Ashlimb to wake from the memory\tYou should return to Ashlimb to wake from the memory.\n",
[7141]="70030527\n1\tTalk to Garmund\tCaptain Garmund can be found just ahead of you, at the northern edge of the farmland. Garmund has asked you to help him repel many of the White Hand trespassers across the farmland.\n",
[7142]="700431B8\n1\tTalk to Angbor\tAngbor can be found inside the Great Hall of Tumladen. You have arrived in the Great Hall and should now speak to Angbor.\n2\tApproach Lady Terenis with Angbor\tLady Terenis and Angbor can be found in the Great Hall of Tumladen. You have arrived in the Great Hall with Angbor, and should now approach Lady Terenis.\n3\tFollow Lord Angbor and Lady Terenis to the fireplace\tLady Terenis and Angbor can be found in the Great Hall of Tumladen. You should follow Lady Terenis and Angbor to the fireplace in the rear of the Great Hall.\n4\tListen as Lord Angbor and Lady Terenis speak\tLady Terenis and Angbor can be found in the Great Hall of Tumladen. Lord Angbor is now speaking with Lady Terenis about the battle at Pelargir. You should listen to their conversation.\n5\tTalk to Lady Terenis\tLady Terenis can be found in the rear of the Great Hall of Tumladen. Lord Angbor has returned to the fields of Lebennin with his host, and has left you to aid Lady Terenis.\n",
[7143]="70071BB6\n1\tTalk to Khagâmi\tKhagâmi is tired from her travels west through An Shêru, and is ready to settle in for the night. Together, you have set up a camp-fire and made yourselves as comfortable as you are able to while on the road.\n2\tInvestigate the sound you heard to the east\tWhile you and Khagâmi were talking at the camp-fire, you both heard a suspicious sound from the east. You should investigate what it was.\n3\tHelp Khagâmi\tWhile you and Khagâmi were talking at the camp-fire, you both fell under attack! You should help Khagâmi.\n4\tDefeat the remaining bandits (total: 4)\tWhile you and Khagâmi were talking at the camp-fire, you both fell under attack! You should defeat the bandits.\n5\tTalk to Faeron\tYou received some unexpected help while defending your camp. You should talk to Faeron.\n",
[7144]="700272C3\n1\tTalk to Léofward to learn his plan\tLéofward is at the Mustering Tree. You should speak with Léofward to learn his plan before the battle begins.\n2\tDefend the Mustering Tree from the Dunlending forces\tDefend the Mustering Tree from the Dunlending forces.\n",
[7145]="700537D1\n1\tTalk to Magoldir\tMagoldir is at Echad-in-Edhil.\n2\tTalk to Glorfindel\tGlorfindel is at Echad-in-Edhil.\n3\tTalk to Lendelen\tLendelen is at Echad-in-Edhil.\n4\tListen to the tale told by the shade of Isildur\tGandalf has interrupted the shade of Isildur's story-telling, bringing you back to the present situation on Tol Send.\n5\tTalk to the shade of Isildur\tThe shade of Isildur has been interrupted by Gandalf, and he is not happy about it.\n6\tListen to the concerns of Gandalf\tGandalf has interrupted the telling of Isildur's tale with a number of questions.\n7\tTalk to the shade of Isildur\tThe shade of Isildur is on Tol Send.\n8\tTalk to Gandalf\tGandalf is on Tol Send.\n",
[7146]="70030231\n1\tTalk to Ingild outside the Elthengels tavern\tYou have run outside the tavern with Ingild, and should speak with him quickly!\n2\tFind Horn in Elthengels\030Find Nona in Elthengels\030Find Corudan in Elthengels\tHorn, Nona, and Corudan are each somewhere in Elthengels. Help them drive off the Orcs!\n3\tDefeat Orcs that remain in Elthengels and then speak with Ingild outside the Mead Hall at the top of the village\tYou have driven off most of the Orcs, but some still remain within Elthengels. Defeat them and then find Ingild outside the Mead Hall at the top of the village.\n4\tTalk to Thane Mildrith outside the Mead Hall in Elthengels\tThane Mildrith is outside the Mead Hall in Elthengels.\n",
[7147]="70064C84\n1\tTalk to Jajax in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl\tYou have returned to Umbar with your brother Jajax.\n2\tFollow Jajax\tYour brother Jajax has asked you to follow him through the city.\n3\tTalk to Jajax in the courtyard of the Teeming Net Tavern\tJajax stands in the courtyard of the Teeming Net Tavern.\n4\tWait in the courtyard for Jajax to return\tJajax has decided to look for information about what has happened in Umbar.\n5\tTalk to Itûr in the courtyard of the Teeming Net Tavern\tYour friend Itûr has recognized you and called you over to him.\n6\tWait for Jajax to return... and cause no trouble\tRemain in the courtyard as your brother Jajax requested, and cause as little trouble as possible.\n7\tTalk to Khôltekh in the courtyard of the Teeming Net Tavern\tKhôltekh has asked you for your name.\n8\tWait for Jajax to return... and cause no trouble\tRemain in the courtyard as your brother Jajax requested, and cause as little trouble as possible.\n9\tTalk to Itûr... quietly\tItûr has quietly caught your attention.\n10\tEscape through the northern exit of the courtyard\tItûr has asked you to discreetly escape from Khôltekh through the northern exit of the courtyard.\n11\tTalk to Jajax outside the courtyard of the Teeming Net Tavern\tJajax has returned to you at great speed. You are not the only sibling to have gotten into trouble!\n12\tFollow Jajax back to the ship... and quickly!\tJajax told you the city is not safe for the two of you, and you have to hurry back to your ship and escape!\n",
[7148]="70046814\n1\tTalk to Gimli north of Cirith Negen\tGimli is standing off the road north of Cirith Negen, waiting to attack the enemy ambushers. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Dagoras north of Cirith Negen\tYou have met up with Dagoras in the woods north of Cirith Negen. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tAttack the Orc leader at Cirith Negen to signal the other Rangers\tYour attack on the Orc leader at Cirith Negen will be the signal for Dagoras and the other Rangers to begin the full assault. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tSurvive combat until the Rangers can attack!\tYou need to survive until the Rangers can finish their attack! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tThe tables have been turned!\tThe Rangers have launched their attack!\n6\tTalk to Dagoras north of Cirith Negen\tYou and the Rangers have turned the tables on the ambushers at Cirith Negen.\n",
[7149]="7005AF6D\n1\tTalk to Kyrstig\tKyrstig waits to speak with you.\n2\tEnter the dwarf-tomb\tKyrstig has pointed out the first tomb on the left in Akhaldarâg as yours. You should enter the tomb.\n3\tClear the tomb of Angmarim\tThe dwarf-tomb contains Angmarim possessed of evil intent.\n4\tTalk to Kyrstig\tKyrstig needs your help.\n5\tConfront Loknashra\tIt is time to confront Loknashra!\n6\tDefeat the Dwarf-wights\tYou should defeat the dwarf-wights in the tomb.\n",
[7150]="700000CF\n1\tTalk to Jon Brackenbrook\tYou stand outside the breach in Archet's east wall, due west of the Hunter's Lodge. You must prevent the Blackwolds from capturing Archet.\n2\tTalk to Ned Pruner\tNed Pruner is grievously wounded and requires assistance.\n3\tTalk to Jon Brackenbrook\tFind a way to get to the centre of Archet and find Amdir. After you defeated the prisoners, Ned Pruner told you that the Blackwold brigands had attempted to invade Archet at last, and that Amdir helped to defend the Inn. Amdir can be found somewhere ahead; you should aid him in the defence of The Mad Badger Inn. After Ned died, his poor wife Peg came to attend to his body.\n4\tTalk to Jon Brackenbrook\tThe Archet market square is blocked, and Jon Brackenbrook is worried that you are too late. He wants to press on.\n5\tTalk to Jon Brackenbrook\tYou were too late to save the crafters' area, but it may not be too late to save all of Archet.\n6\tDefeat the Blackwolds and their leader\tProtect Archet by defeating the Blackwolds' invasion. Amdir was rendered powerless by the morgul-wound he suffered from the Nazgûl, and now it is up to you to save Archet from the Blackwolds.\n7\tTalk to Jon Brackenbrook\tWith Archet saved, you should speak with Jon Brackenbrook.\n",
[7151]="7002825B\n1\tTalk to Bedwur\tMany merchants have gathered here tonight.\n2\tObserve the auction\tMany merchants have gathered here tonight.\n3\tTalk to Bedwur\tMany merchants have gathered here tonight.\n",
[7152]="7004484F\n1\tJoin the Finder's Gathering\tJoin the children at the table for the Finder's Gathering.\n2\tTake part in the Gathering\tTake part in the Finder's Gathering with Bergil and the other children.\n3\tTalk to Gelwen\tGelwen has stumbled into the room, troubled and out of breath. Talk to her to find out what has happened.\n4\tTalk to Gelwen\tYou have come with Gelwen and Bergil to the cisterns. See if Gelwen can retrace her steps and to find her brother Glatham.\n5\tSearch for Glatham\tYou have come with Gelwen and Bergil to the cisterns. Go with them and find Glatham.\n6\tDefeat the goblins\tYou have found Glatham, surrounded by goblins! More goblins come in through a breach in the wall.\n7\tDefeat the goblin captain\tBy dispatching the goblins near Glatham and the strange woman, you have caught the attention of the goblin captain.\n8\tTalk to Gelwen\tGelwen stands with Bergil, Glatham, and the mysterious woman near where the goblins came in. You have defeated the goblins who made a breach into this part of the cisterns and for the moment, it is safe. You should see what Gelwen has to say.\n",
[7153]="70010042\n1\tTalk to Faelbenn\tReceive your orders from Faelbenn.\n2\tDefeat Angmarim sorceresses ([see journal]/5)\tDefeat the Angmarim sorceresses and prevent the reinforcements from crossing Rammas Deluon. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tTalk to Faelbenn\tVictory is yours... you should speak again with Faelbenn at once.\n",
[7154]="70049414\n1\tYou are a Lothlórien sentry, keeping watch over the Golden Wood. You should join your fellow sentry up ahead.\t\n2\tDefend Lothlórien from Orcs and trolls\tOrc invaders have appeared in Lothlórien! Help defend the Golden Wood.\n3\tPush onward to the east and defeat the Orc-invaders\tOrc invaders have appeared in Lothlórien! Push onward to where the fighting appears worst.\n4\tHead east and protect Galadriel while she readies her defences\tOrc invaders have appeared in Lothlórien and now Lady Galadriel has taken to the field. Fight by her side and guard her at all costs.\n5\tTalk to Galadriel\tGaladriel has used her powers to defeat the last of this Orc assault. Now she wishes to talk to you.\n6\tDefeat Orc-invaders in Mirkwood by the lamp-posts in the wood\tYou have arrived in Mirkwood and come to the edge of the fighting.\n7\tHead east and talk to King Thranduil\tYou have arrived in Mirkwood. You have crossed paths with Lord Thranduil himself, and should talk with him.\n8\tFollow the archers to the north-east, up the hill\tKing Thranduil asked you to follow the archers to the north-east, up the hill.\n9\tDefeat every attacking enemy on the hilltop. This is the last stand!\tYou have come to a hilltop in Mirkwood held by Elves and embattled on all sides. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n10\tTalk to Thranduil on the hilltop\tYou have crossed paths with Lord Thranduil once again in Mirkwood.\n",
[7155]="70010041\n1\tTalk to Firingal\tSpeak to Firingal regarding the defence of Aughaire.\n2\tDefend Aughaire\tDefend Aughaire from Angmar's assault. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tTalk to Firingal\tYou should report back to Firingal.\n",
[7156]="70027A67\n1\tTalk to Grimbold\030Destroy Dunlending banners (total: 4)\030Defeat the Dunlending chieftain (quantity: see journal)\tDefend against the Dunlendings atop Dol Baran.\n2\tTalk to Grimbold atop Dol Baran\tGrimbold awaits you atop Dol Baran. You should speak with Grimbold regarding your victory.\n3\tSee to the dead atop Dol Baran\tSee to the dead atop Dol Baran.\n",
[7157]="70019014\n1\tTalk to Belvagor\tBelvagor is at the base of the slope that climbs up into Fanuidhol. The Elf Belvagor is waiting to speak with you about his plan for repelling the Orc-attack.\n2\tBelvagor and his two friends wait for orders on the slope that climbs up into Fanuidhol. Belvagor and his two friends wait for you to tell them which passes to defend. To do this, you should first travel to the Northern Pass, Western Pass, and Eastern Pass and note the composition of the defenders at each; then you can make an informed decision.\t\n3\tDestroy Idols of the Enemy ([see journal]/4)\tThe Orc-attack is underway! You must work together with your allies to carry a Banner of Lórien to the four Orc-encampments so the Idol of the Enemy at each can be destroyed, and you must do it before any of the three passes can be overrun. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tTalk to Belvagor\tYou have destroyed four Idols of the Enemy and should return now to speak with Belvagor at the pass you told him to defend.\n",
[7158]="70010043\n1\tTalk to Tordoron\tSpeak with Tordoron to receive your marching orders.\n2\tClaim all of Angmar's encampments ([see journal]/4)\t This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tTalk to Tordoron\tYou should speak with Tordoron regarding your victory.\n",
[7159]="70014670\n1\tSpeak to Brogur\tYou should speak to Brogur to see of what aid you might be in the coming battle.\n2\tDefend the Deep-way\tHelp hold the Deep-way against the Mazog's assault. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tDefeat Horngoth and his minions\tThe warleader of the assault against the Deep-way has entered the battle. You must strike this Orc down and claim victory. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tSpeak to Brogur\tWith Horngoth defeated, the battle of the Deep-way has been won. Speak to Brogur to see what else he would have you do.\n",
[7160]="7002AD6E\n1\tTalk to Grimbold\tYou have come down the road in retreat with Grimbold, and he has put up his hand to stop you.\n2\tFight off the attacking forces in order to buy Théodred precious time to retreat\tYou have retreated further down the road and are once more embroiled in the fighting. You must buy Théodred as much time as you can!\n3\tTalk to Grimbold\tGrimbold has fought off his opponent and wants to speak with you while he catches his breath.\n4\tTalk to Grimbold\tThe men are disorganized and in chaos, and Grimbold wants to gather them together for one last stand.\n5\tTalk to Grimbold\tA rider has brought disturbing news: a second force of uruks has left Isengard in secret and has driven the defending force at the Ford of Isen back into Rohan.\n",
[7161]="7002AD70\n1\tTalk to Grimbold\tGrimbold needs you to fight alongside him to where Théodred is suffering the fierce attacks of Saruman's forces.\n2\tTalk to Grimbold on the bank of the Isen\tPrince Théodred is in trouble on the eyot in the middle of the Isen! You need to fight alongside Grimbold to come to the aid of the Prince!\n3\tConfront Morflak\tYou have come to the eyot in the middle of the river Isen and have found the uruk Morflak gloating over Théodred's fallen form.\n4\tTalk to Morflak\tYou have come to the eyot in the middle of the river Isen and have found the uruk Morflak gloating over Théodred's fallen form.\n",
[7162]="70014672\n1\tSpeak to Wíli\tSpeak to Wíli to see what aid you might lend in his defence.\n2\tDefend the Twenty-first Hall\tHelp hold the Twenty-first Hall against Mazog's assault. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tFall back and defend the hall barricades\tGoblin-sappers have destroyed the barriers at the Twenty-first Hall's barricades. Wíli has sounded a retreat to the hall outside the Chamber of Mazarbul. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tFall back and defend the Chamber of Mazarbul\tOnce more, goblin-sappers have destroyed the barriers at the barricades. Wíli has called a retreat to the Chamber of Mazarbul. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tSpeak to Wíli\tWith the Orcs driven off, you should speak to Wíli to see if there is anything else he would have you do.\n",
[7163]="70014671\n1\tSpeak to Stóthkell\tSpeak to Stóthkell to see what aid you might lend in the defence.\n2\tFollow Stóthkell\tFollow Stóthkell to learn the source of what is shaking the Way of the Smiths.\n3\tDefend the Smithway\tHelp hold the Way of Smiths against Mazog's assault. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tSpeak to Stóthkell\tWith the Orcs driven off, you should speak to Stóthkell to see if there is anything else he would have you do.\n",
[7164]="7006A889\n1\tTalk to Corudan in the forgotten passage\tCorudan stands in a forgotten passage within Kamrabezûr.\n2\tTalk to Sigileth in the forgotten passage\tSigileth waits for you and Corudan in the forgotten passage.\n3\tStand your ground!\tThe passage shakes as a mighty beast charges toward you and your friends down the forgotten passage!\n4\tTalk to Corudan in the forgotten passage\tCorudan stands in a forgotten passage within Kamrabezûr.\n5\tFollow Corudan and Sigileth down the forgotten passage\tDespite the appearance of the rampaging beast, Corudan and Sigileth have not abandoned their purpose to investigate the forgotten passage within Kamrabezûr.\n6\tTalk to the dying Umbari woman\tJudging from the quantity of blood spilled on the floor of this chamber, the Umbari woman does not have long to live.\n7\tListen to Cruel Dancer's story\tListen to what befell Cruel Dancer when she caught up to Tatháta in the forgotten passage within Kamrabezûr.\n8\tTalk to Cruel Dancer and hear her last request\tCruel Dancer lies dying in the forgotten passage within Kamrabezûr.\n9\tTalk to Corudan in the forgotten passage within Kamrabezûr\tCorudan stands in the forgotten passage within Kamrabezûr.\n10\tBring Galatâni into the sunlight before she dies\tGalatâni asked that you bring her outside into the sunlight before she dies.\n11\tTalk to Galatâni in the moonlight\tGalatâni lies dying in the moonlight.\n12\tStand with Galatâni and observe her final moments\tGalatâni does not have much time to live.\n13\tHear what Galatâni has left to say\tGalatâni has one more thing to say to you.\n",
[7165]="700479FE\n1\tTalk to Aragorn outside the Black Gate\tAragorn is at the Morannon, the Black Gate of Mordor, and prepares to challenge Sauron.\n2\tStand with Aragorn as he defies the Dark Lord Sauron\tAragorn has decided to call for the surrender of Sauron, and wishes for you to stand with him.\n3\tStand with Aragorn as he defies the Mouth of Sauron\tThe Mouth of Sauron has presented tokens for the perusal of the company.\n4\tTalk to Pippin and keep him quiet\tMithrandir has asked you to make Pippin hold his tongue lest he endanger the negotiations with the Mouth of Sauron.\n5\tListen to the demands of the Mouth of Sauron\tThe Mouth of Sauron mocks the Host of the West, and prepares the terms of Aragorn's surrender. Remain alert.\n6\tTalk to Mithrandir\tMithrandir has asked for you to speak with him while he considers Sauron's terms.\n7\tCollect the short-sword\030Collect the Elf-cloak\030Collect the mithril-shirt\tMithrandir asked you to retrieve the items presented by the Mouth of Sauron.\n8\tStand with the Host of the West in defiance of Mordor\tYou have taken the items that belonged to Frodo and Sam, and Gandalf has defied the Mouth of Sauron.\n",
[7166]="70009672\n1\tTalk to Aragorn\tAragorn is waiting to speak with you just outside the forges of Rivendell. Elf-smiths are reforging Narsil, the blade that was broken.\n2\tWitness the reforging of Narsil\tAt the forges of Rivendell, the Elf-smiths of Elrond are hard at work remaking the sword of the kings. Elf-smiths have begun the work of reforging Narsil.\n3\tTalk to Aragorn\tAragorn is at the forges of Rivendell. Aragorn wishes to speak with you.\n",
[7167]="70034288\n1\tSit by the fire with your companions\tYour companions are sitting around the fire in Nona's cave, and you should do the same. Simply sit by the fire and relax while you can.\n2\tRelax around the fire with your companions\tYour companions are relaxing around the fire in Nona's cave, having earned a small, and overdue, respite.\n3\tTalk to Nona inside the cave\tNona has leapt to her feet, and wants to see what you think of the rumbling sound.\n4\tJoin Nona outside the cave\tYou have come outside with your companions to see what has happened.\n5\tWatch the mighty force leaving Balewood\tA mighty force of Huorns are leaving the Balewood. They can have only one destination: Núrzum!\n6\tTalk to Corudan on the slope outside the cave\tYour companions are transfixed by the sight. Only Corudan can manage the words to describe it.\n",
[7168]="7005242F\n1\tTalk to Haerandel\tHaerandel desires to speak to you of the legendary flower Anarlossë, long vanished from Middle-earth.\n2\tListen to Haerandel's tale of the legendary Anarlossë\tHaerandel desires to speak to you of the legendary flower Anarlossë, long vanished from Middle-earth.\n3\tTalk to Mílgamel\tMílgamel has some questions to ask about Haerandel's tale.\n4\tTalk to Nethlas\tNethlas puts more stock in the words of his master than in those of Haerandel, and is not too shy to say so.\n5\tTalk to Haerandel\tHaerandel desires to speak to you of the legendary flower Anarlossë, long vanished from Middle-earth.\n6\tListen to Haerandel's tale of the legendary Anarlossë\tHaerandel desires to speak to you of the legendary flower Anarlossë, long vanished from Middle-earth.\n7\tTalk to Haerandel\tHaerandel has told you of the legendary flower Anarlossë.\n",
})
